{
  "about": "Golden vectors of an upload's manifest, version 1 (internal/accountcrypto/manifest.go, plan §9): the browser's workers and the CLI are held to them. Bytes are hex. The manifest key is HKDF-SHA-256 Expand of the file key (the password's Argon2id output) with the label as info, 32 bytes; the sealed manifest is the magic, a 24-byte nonce and XChaCha20-Poly1305 of the padded records with the label and the token as additional data. Padded: records' length (uint32 big-endian), records (type byte, uint32 big-endian length, value), zeros to 256*2^j bytes (any multiple of 256 up to 64 KiB opens). Type 1: SHA-256s, 32 bytes a file. Type 2: the upload's reply key, SHA3-256 of its public key, 32 bytes. An opener skips an unknown type and refuses type 0, a type twice, a record past the length, an empty or uneven list, a reply key of other than 32 bytes, non-zero padding, more than 64 KiB. Every opens case with ok=false must be refused; an opens case with zeros instead of sealed is that many zero bytes, sealed as they are with its nonce. go test ./internal/accountcrypto -run TestManifestVectors -update writes this file anew.",
